# BurnhopeEngine Architectural Constitution

Be uncompromising and thorough. Build fault-tolerant systems. Ship complete, compilable code.
No ad-hoc glue, one-off workarounds, fake stubs, placeholders, `// TODO`, or `// ... rest unchanged ...`.
No warning pragmas to hide a violation. No `const_cast` to break a const contract. No `reinterpret_cast` across non-trivial types. No `void*` adapter when a type is in the wrong layer: move the type down to the layer that may legally own it.
A module is a black box: it owns its memory, lifecycle, and typed interface. Siblings do not mutate each other's internals, share ad-hoc mutable memory, or trigger hidden work in an unrelated subsystem. A failure stays inside that subsystem's recovery contract (`BH_ASSERT` in debug, typed `false` / error to the caller).

This file is the single architectural law. When a bug is fixed, append one line: `NEVER [banned action] (causes [failure]); ALWAYS [alternative] [exact slots, bytes, alignment].` Do not restate a ban that already exists.

---

## 1. Mission

BurnhopeEngine is a from-scratch 3D engine and declarative GUI. Layer 3 must read like one line of Qt/Slate. The machine path is AAA: Vulkan 1.4, data-oriented layout, Flecs, C++26, AVX2.

Desktop x86_64 only (Linux and Windows, AVX2). No mobile, WebAssembly-as-a-target, or legacy OS. (The in-engine `core/wasm/WasmHost` bytecode interpreter is engine code; it is not a Web target.)

Axioms:

1. **Zero hot-path allocation.** `Tick`, `Layout`, `Emit`, `Draw`, `Consume`, and `HitTest` do not call `malloc`, `free`, `new`, `delete`, `realloc`, `std::string`, `std::vector::push_back`, `std::map`, `std::unordered_map`, or `std::make_shared`. Per-frame memory comes from `core/memory/FrameArena.hpp` (reset in O(1)), a ring buffer, a fixed stack array, or `UiVirtualPool`.
2. **DOD.** Hot data is trivially copyable POD, `sizeof % 16 == 0` or `sizeof % 64 == 0`, with `alignas(16)` / `alignas(64)` and `static_assert` on the GPU size. Prefer SoA and flat arrays. Trees and ASTs use `uint16_t` / `uint32_t` or `flecs::entity`, never `Node*`, `std::vector<Node*>`, or `std::unique_ptr<Node>`. Hot fields sit together; cold strings sit apart.
3. **Zero-copy I/O.** Assets, SPIR-V, layouts, and textures load through `fileMapReadOnly` (`core/io/File.hpp`: `mmap` / `MapViewOfFile`). Numbers use `std::from_chars`. Formatting uses `core/Str.hpp`, `std::to_chars`, or a bounded `snprintf` on the stack. No `sscanf`, no locale CRT parsers, no `std::string` concatenation.
4. **ECS composition.** A widget or actor is a `flecs::entity` (or a 16-bit id) plus POD components. No vtables, no `QObject` / MOC, no ImGui, no immediate-mode GUI.
5. **Vulkan 1.4 only.** Dynamic rendering, shader objects, mesh shaders, bindless descriptor heaps, BDA. Legacy Vulkan listed in §7 is banned.

---

## 2. Four-layer pyramid (`N → <N`)

Every file has exactly one layer. A file may include, forward-declare, name, or call only a strictly lower layer. No cycles. No upward leak. Banning an include in the `.hpp` and adding it in the `.cpp` is the same violation.

```
LAYER 3  Domain tools and apps
         demo/app/  core/files/  core/host/  editor/scene tools
         Declarative coordinators, under 350 LOC (prefer under 300).
         Sees layers 2, 1, and 0. Zero RHI, Yoga, and vertex internals.
LAYER 2  Generic widgets
         core/ui/widget/  core/ui/kit/  core/ui/Panel
         POD config structs, Flecs components, Yoga styles.
         Zero knowledge of files, scenes, or the editor.
         Sets components only. Never writes UiPrimitive* or Vulkan commands.
LAYER 1  UI infrastructure
         core/ui/ (State, Layout, LayoutBridge, PrimitiveBatch, Font, Canvas, Motion)
         core/ui/rhi/ (UiRenderer)
         UiState holds only the Flecs world, node tree, focus, and design tokens.
         Zero knowledge of Button, Tree, Grid, Menu, Splitter, or any tool.
         Node, Hit, Input, Focus, Text, PrimitiveBatch, Layout, and Json are infrastructure
         even when a file currently sits under widget/.
LAYER 0  Hardware, OS, memory, I/O
         core/rhi/  core/platform/  core/io/  core/image/  core/memory/
         core/gfx/  core/asset/  core/stream/  core/wasm/  core/time/
         core/doc/  core/debug/  core/text/  core/color/  core/anim/  core/input/  core/Str.hpp
         Standard library, OS, Vulkan. Zero UI, Yoga, widgets, files/, or editor/.
GRAPHICS engine/  (gpu_scene/, include/render/, src/, shader/)
         Built on layer 0. Zero UI, Yoga, widgets, and app domain.
         Scene Flecs lives in engine/gpu_scene. core/rhi and core/platform have zero ECS.
```

Laws:

- **Layer 0 blindness.** `core/rhi` never includes `platform/Window.hpp`. `deviceCreate` takes a raw `VkSurfaceKHR`. Timing lives in `core/platform/PlatformUtil.hpp`. `InputFrame` lives in `core/platform/Input.hpp`. `core/ui/PrimitiveBatch.cpp` never includes `<yoga/Yoga.h>`; visibility is `nodeShown(s, p)` plus the `s.culled[p]` bitmask.
- **Layer 1 generalization.** Infrastructure never includes a widget or Domain header. `Node.cpp`, `PrimitiveBatch.cpp`, `Json.cpp`, `Layout.cpp`, and `Input.cpp` register draw, overlay, input, spawn, and role-finish hooks. They do not name Tree, Button, or File APIs.
- **Layer 2 agnosticism.** Widgets take abstract models, callbacks, and Flecs components. No `"list_inner"`, `"status"`, `"BistroScene"`, demo drag-reorder, or hardcoded slots in `Input.cpp`, `Tree.cpp`, or `List.cpp`.
- **Layer 3 facades.** Layer 3 never writes `UiState.field`, `menu`, `fieldMenu`, `topOn`, `ghost`, `opOpacity`, `contextOf`, `parentOf`, `altLook`, `layoutDirty`, `visualDirty`, `opMinimize`, or `opMaximize`. Call `uiSetField`, `uiSetMenu`, `uiSetFieldMenu`, `uiRequestTop`, `uiRequestOpacity`, `uiSetContextMenu`, `uiParent`, `uiApplyLook`, `uiNotifyLayoutDirty`, `uiNotifyVisualDirty`, `uiRequestMinimize`, `uiRequestMaximize`. Host chrome goes through `windowMinimize(host, slot)` / `windowMaximize(host, slot)`.
- A render pass never includes `ui/Model.hpp`.

Canonical Layer 3 shape:

```cpp
auto [treePane, gridPane] = uiSplitter(s, rootNode, { .width = 240.0f });
uiFolderTree(s, treePane, {
    .model = &fileModel,
    .onSelect = [&](const auto& path) { fileModel.navigateTo(path); }
});
uiVirtualGrid(s, gridPane, {
    .items = fileModel.currentEntries(),
    .onActivate = [&](size_t idx) { fileModel.execute(idx); }
});
```

---

## 3. Single source of truth

If two modules share setup, layout, or parsing: do not copy it, and do not let peer A call peer B. Push the shared code to a lower layer.

| Concern | Authority |
| :--- | :--- |
| JSON | `core/io/JsonCursor.hpp`, `core/io/Json.hpp` (zero-copy, `\uXXXX`, scientific notation). No second parser. |
| Strings and numbers | `core/Str.hpp`, `std::from_chars`, `std::to_chars` |
| Input snapshot | `core/platform/Input.hpp`. No second mouse, key, or gamepad queue. |
| Virtualization | `core/ui/widget/Virtual.hpp`: `UiVirtualBase`, `uiVirtualTotalHeight`, `UiVirtualPool`, `kUiPoolCap`. Scroll, grid, and tree all use it. |
| Text measure and wrap | `uiWrapCut` for labels and fields |
| Files | `fileMapReadOnly`. No `fread` into a heap vector, no `std::ifstream` on runtime assets, no `fopen`/`fclose` probe before load. A failed map is the missing-file path. |
| Images | `core/image/`: decode from the mapped span (SDR, HDR, GIF, DDS). Compress BC1/BC3/BC4/BC5/BC7/BC6H. Upload via Host Image Copy or staging. |
| Time, cache, exe path | `core/platform/PlatformUtil.hpp` |
| Shader directory | `engine/include/render/RenderDefs.hpp`. Never copy `#ifndef BH_SHADER_DIR` into a pass. |
| Shader math | `engine/shader/core/` and `engine/shader/camera.slang` only |
| Descriptor slots | `core/rhi/DescriptorSlots.hpp` |
| Field setup | `uiFieldInit` in `core/ui/widget/Field.cpp` |
| Node names | `uiName` / `uiFindName` in Layer 1 `Node`. Lookup only while building, never inside `engineTick`. |
| Hotkeys | `core/platform/Action.hpp` |
| Asserts | `core/platform/Check.hpp` (`BH_ASSERT`, cpptrace) |
| Tracy | `core/platform/Trace.hpp` |
| CPU spikes | `core/debug/CpuScope.hpp` |

Header hygiene: a file includes only the headers it uses. `Detail.hpp` does not include every widget header. POSIX headers (`<sys/mman.h>`, `<unistd.h>`, `<fcntl.h>`, `<spawn.h>`, `<dlfcn.h>`, `<dirent.h>`, `<sys/stat.h>`) never appear in a platform-agnostic header; a `.cpp` that must use them guards with `#if !defined(_WIN32)`.

C++26 dialect: designated initializers on every aggregate. Non-owning arguments are `std::string_view` or `std::span<const T>`. Constraints are concepts, not `std::enable_if_t`.

---

## 4. Flecs

Components are POD. No logic in component constructors or destructors. Behavior is free functions and Flecs queries. Child lifetime is the `ChildOf` relationship, not a hand-rolled recursive free.

- Hot loops read `flecs::column<T>`. No `entity.get<T>()` or `try_get<T>()` in `Tick`, `Layout`, `Emit`, `Draw`, or cull.
- A single-entity hit or write reads `Xform` on `world.ent[index]`. Never `actorLoad` the whole set into a stack buffer first.
- Worlds are unbounded. `std::vector<flecs::entity>` and `sceneActorAdd`. Never `kSceneActorCap`, `flecs::entity ent[16]`, or any fixed entity ceiling.
- Widget identity is a component: `UiSplitter`, `UiTitleBar`, `UiMenuBar`, `UiResizable`, `UiImage`. Clicks go through `uiBind` of a `UiAction`. Multi-stop gradients set `paint.ramp = kRampColorWheel`.
- Banned identities: paint tags and magic integers `-5`, `-6`, `-7`, `-15`, `-90`, `-70..-78`, `-100`, and any `tag == N` / `type == 999` sentinel.
- Button, Check, and Field are one entity that owns its `UiText` and `UiPaint`. Never spawn a child Label and patch its box with `placeChromeText` or `fieldPlaceText`.
- `Hit.cpp` tests `hitBox` only. `scrollThumb` and `splitGrip` run in the widget input hook.
- A widget never writes `UiHostNote`. Publish `ColorBook.present` (`uiSetColorBook`).

Banned fake pools: `wTree[12]`, `wCell[18]`, `crumbs.seg[8]`, `pop.row[12]`, `UiNode treeSlots[12]`, `char pathSegments[8][64]`. Visible rows come from `UiVirtualPool`. Ten items and ten million items share the same recycler (about thirty live slots).

---

## 5. UI contracts

Chrome, borders, fills, and accents use tokens:

```cpp
paintToken(s.look, UiRole::Button, UiToken::Button, s.look.radiusSm);
paint->token = static_cast<uint8_t>(isSelected ? UiToken::Accent : UiToken::Item);
```

No raw RGB floats (`paint.r = 0.15f`) in Layers 2 or 3, including `Shell.cpp` and `Sample.cpp`. Theme changes go through `uiApplyLook` / `uiRestyle`. Palette variation reads `s.look.accent[i]`.

Layout:

- Never put a 100% width `uiSlider` in a horizontal row beside a label (Yoga collapses it to 0). Stack vertically.
- Role `Scroll` requires `UiScroll.inner`.
- `cacheBox` is O(1) from the parent bounds. Do not walk ancestors to the root.
- `uiLayout` is O(N): inspect Yoga flex-drop children directly. No O(N²) full-tree rescan.
- Every container clips through the core scissor manager.

Coordinates scale by `canvas.dpi`. No assumed `1920×1080`, 60 Hz, or DPI 1.0.

One UI draw per frame: `vkCmdDraw` or `vkCmdDrawMeshTasksEXT` from the mapped host-visible SSBO ring. `core/ui/rhi/UiRenderer` binds that buffer at slot 48.

Preserve behavior while splitting files. Required features stay, moved into the right Layer 2 widget: context menus, inline F2 rename, rubberband selection, Ctrl/Shift modifiers, hierarchy chevrons, forward/back history, docking, form validation.

---

## 6. Frame phases (`core/host/Host.cpp`)

```
Phase 1 main          Phase 2 jobsRunAndWait       Phase 3 main
SDL poll, DPI,        Yoga, Flecs, SSBO batch,     deferred callbacks,
resize, arena reset,  command buffers              clipboard, vkQueueSubmit2,
input snapshot                                     timeline wait, vkQueuePresentKHR
```

Phase 2 workers never call SDL, change window state, read the clipboard, or run `onDrop` / `onOps`. Those callbacks are queued for Phase 3.

`jobsRunAndWait` holds its mutex until workers finish. Wait on `idle` until `current == nullptr` and `engaged == 0`. Do not publish the next batch over a live one.

`platformPace(hz, uint64_t& nextTick)` stores the deadline on the window (`host.paceNext`). No function-local `static` clock, and no `static` mutable state in any function. State lives on `Host`, `UiState`, or the window.

No `std::this_thread::sleep_for`, spin-sleep, or lock-free polling used as a sync protocol. Sync is timeline semaphores, a wait-free ring, or a condition variable with a real predicate.

Clipboard text is read on explicit paste (Ctrl+V). Never call `SDL_GetClipboardText` at the end of every frame.

---

## 7. Vulkan 1.4

Required: `vkCmdBeginRendering` / `vkCmdEndRendering`, `VK_EXT_shader_object` via `vkCmdBindShadersEXT`, `VK_EXT_mesh_shader` via `vkCmdDrawMeshTasksEXT`, `VK_EXT_descriptor_heap` plus BDA, `vkCmdPipelineBarrier2`, timeline semaphores, Host Image Copy. Lighting is radiance cascades, a clustered light grid, and two-phase GPU Hi-Z.

Banned:

- `VkRenderPass`, `VkFramebuffer`, runtime `VkPipeline`, `vkCreateGraphicsPipelines`.
- `VkDescriptorPool`, `VkDescriptorSet`, `vkCmdPipelineBarrier` (v1), binary fences per pass.
- `vkDeviceWaitIdle` and CPU fence waits inside the frame loop and on resize.
- `VK_KHR_mesh_shader` (use `VK_EXT_mesh_shader`).
- `vkCmdUpdateBuffer` for per-dispatch constants.
- `VkPipelineLayout` stored on a shader-object pass. After bind, `vkCmdPushConstants` with `VK_NULL_HANDLE`. The push block is 16 bytes.

Submission: the scene ends color on `LOAD_CLEAR` and signals only `uiSem`. The canvas waits `uiSem`, begins with `LOAD` (`LOAD_OP_LOAD`), transitions the swapchain image to `VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_PRESENT_SRC_KHR`, and signals present. The scene never calls `swapchainToPresent`.

`shaderCreate` failure destroys the pass and returns `false`. A missing optional device feature (no ray query) may stay off and return `true`. Do not return success for a shader that failed to compile.

### 7.1 Slots and POD sizes

- UI primitive SSBO: descriptor slot **48** (`kUiDescPrims` in `core/rhi/DescriptorSlots.hpp`, canvas range 48..63). Scene passes never write slot 48.
- SDF font atlas: slot **661**. UI photos: slots **662–669**.
- `HeapBuf::Rc` is slot **18**. Radiance cascades use slot 18.
- `GizmoGpu`: **320** bytes (multiple of 64).
- `FrameView`: **384** bytes, binding 0.
- `FrameSun`: **1920** bytes, binding 49, `HeapBuf::Sun`.
- Slider blocks: bindings **50–57**, **64** bytes each.
- `AtmosphereParams`: `float pad[26]` (**192** bytes). Never `z0`..`z25`.
- `InstanceData`: **80** bytes.

### 7.2 One shader, push the index

Never compile a second SPIR-V per flight, Hi-Z mip, cubemap face, shadow cascade, or point light. Banned names: `CULL_FLIGHT`, `HIZ_MIP`, `CUBE_FACE`, `visbuffer.shadow0/1/2`, `visbuffer.point0/1/2`, `cube0..5`, `bloom0..3`. One shader. A 16-byte push selects the slot:

- `flight`, or `flight + mip`
- `face + stride`
- `cascade` into `HeapBuf::ShadowAll` at binding 18
- `light` into the full `PointVisible` list at binding 19

Index the heap as `base_slot + push.index`.

### 7.3 Images and resize

Accumulation (`hdrA` through Sun → Lamps → Reflect → Fog → Clouds → Radiance): `discard = true` only on the first transition of an uninitialized image (`oldLayout = UNDEFINED`). Every later barrier uses `discard = false` and `oldLayout = tracked.layout`.

After `framePassVis`, vis and depth leave attachment layout. `release()` them to `SHADER_READ_ONLY`, including the late draw.

Resize does not call `sceneFrameReleaseGpu` and does not destroy static vertex buffers, instance buffers, BLAS, or material textures. Recreate transient targets only — vis, depth, shade, cloud, Hi-Z, bloom (`Vis`, `Depth`, `HdrA`, `HdrB`, `Ao`, `Contact`, `Reflect`, `HiZMax`, `Bloom`) — then `bindHeap` in O(1).

Blend: additive is `SRC = ONE`, `DST = ONE`. Multiply is `SRC = DST_COLOR`, `DST = ZERO`.

`meshletPackNormal` is octahedral and keeps Z. Hi-Z occlusion samples a conservative 2×2 footprint. The cluster grid may be 16×9×24 cells; world positions are transformed by the scene AABB. Never treat the world as a fixed 16×9×24 meter box.

Volumetric noise is one GPU dispatch of `cloud_noise.comp` into `HeapBuf::CloudNoise`. Never fill a 128³ Worley volume on the CPU.

HUD and tick code use cached `uint16_t` ids (`HudIds`: `mode[20]`, `stat[12]`, and the slider ids). No `snprintf` and no `uiFindName` inside `engineTick`. HUD hit records live on `Engine::hud` as a `std::deque`. No global `T[8]` / `T[16]`.

Scene CPU buffers (`meshletGpu`, `visibleCpu`, `ownedVert`, `textures`) are `std::vector`. No `new[]` / `delete[]`.

---

## 8. Platform and assets

- User directory: `platformUserDir` (`USERPROFILE` on Windows, `HOME` on Linux). Cache file: `platformCachePath` (`%LOCALAPPDATA%` / `%USERPROFILE%` on Windows, `$HOME/.cache/` on Linux). Executable: `platformExePath` (`GetModuleFileNameA` / `/proc/self/exe`). Host meters: `platformHostMeters`.
- Never call `getenv("HOME")`, `readlink("/proc/self/exe")`, or `/proc` from app, scene, or render code.
- Directories: `std::filesystem::create_directories` and `std::filesystem::directory_iterator`. No `mkdir(path, 0755)`, no `<dirent.h>`.
- Process launch lives in `core/platform/Desktop.cpp`: `posix_spawnp` on Linux, `ShellExecuteA` / `CreateProcessA` on Windows. Never concatenate a command and pass it to `sh -c`.
- Dynamic libraries: `LoadLibraryA` on Windows and `dlopen` on Linux, behind the platform loader. No raw `<dlfcn.h>` in engine or render code.
- Dialogs: `core/platform/Dialog.cpp` (SDL3). Windowing: `core/platform/Window.cpp` (SDL3). The window system is SDL3.
- No hardcoded absolute paths (`/home/...`, `C:\Users\...`) and no hardcoded screen size. Resolve from `platformExePath`, the project root, and `platformCachePath`.
- Textures resolve in order: beside the active `.bhop`, then the adjacent `textures/` directory, then `assets/textures/`, then `uploadDummy`. Never hardcode `newscenetest` or `testscene/assets/bistro` inside a pass.
- A missing `.bhop` keeps the procedural scene from `sceneFrameCreate` / `testSceneBuild`. Never import a hardcoded glTF (`BistroExterior`) as a fallback.
- Parsers are bounds-checked and must terminate on bad syntax. No fake fallback UI card (`kFallback` is banned).

---

## 9. Canonical modules

Use these homes. Do not invent a parallel `src/` tree.

**App.** `demo/app/Main.cpp` entry. `Engine.hpp/.cpp` window, scene, canvas, cached control ids, host meters, scene load, file drop. `Shell.hpp/.cpp` menus, inspector, tabs, docking, extra windows. `demo/Sample.cpp` nested lists, compact rows, context menus, field validation.

**GPU scene.** `engine/gpu_scene/`: `Mat4.hpp` (column-major, reverse-Z), `Camera.hpp`, `LightMath.hpp`, `InstanceData.hpp`, `InstanceCull.hpp` (SSE2 frustum, LOD0), `MeshletGpu.hpp`, `MeshletCull.hpp`, `PointShadow.hpp`, `SunShadow.hpp`, `SceneObject.hpp` (Flecs actors, gizmo math). `core/scene/FlyCam.hpp`.

**Render.** `engine/include/render/`: `RenderDefs.hpp`, `HeapBind.hpp`, `FrameUniforms.hpp`, `PassCommon.hpp`, `PassAllocators.hpp`, `PassBufferSync.hpp`, `PassRendering.hpp`, `PassShaderGroup.hpp`, `PassTargets.hpp`, `PassDebug.hpp`, `VisResolve.hpp`, `SceneFrame.hpp` / `SceneFrameImpl.hpp`, `Cube.hpp`, `Cull.hpp`, `Hiz.hpp`, `Gizmo.hpp`, `Radiance.hpp`, `Shade.hpp`, `Sky.hpp`, `Tonemap.hpp`, `Visbuffer.hpp`. Translation units: `engine/src/SceneFrame.cpp`, `Cube.cpp`, `Cull.cpp`, `Hiz.cpp`, `PassGizmo.cpp`, `Radiance.cpp`, `Shade.cpp`, `Sky.cpp`, `Tonemap.cpp`, `Visbuffer.cpp`, `PassClusters.cpp`, `PassCull.cpp`, `PassPoints.cpp`, `PassRadiance.cpp`, `PassShade.cpp`, `PassSun.cpp`, `PassTonemap.cpp`, `PassVis.cpp`.

**Platform and I/O.** `core/platform/`: `Check`, `Trace`, `Window`, `Dialog`, `Desktop`, `Input`, `Action`, `Jobs`, `PlatformUtil`. `core/debug/CpuScope.hpp`. `core/memory/FrameArena.hpp`. `core/io/`: `File`, `Blob`, `JsonCursor`, `Json`. `core/Str.hpp`. `core/color/Color.hpp` (RGBA8, sRGB↔linear, HSV). `core/time/Time.hpp`. `core/doc/UndoStack.hpp`, `Document.hpp`. `core/wasm/WasmHost.hpp`.

**RHI and images.** `core/rhi/`: `VolkVma.cpp`, `DeviceCaps`, `Device`, `GpuBuffer`, `GpuImage`, `Barrier`, `DescriptorHeap`, `DescriptorSlots`, `ShaderObject`, `Swapchain`, `MeshDraw`, `GpuProfiler`. `core/image/`: `ImageDecode`, `ImageCompress`, `ImageUpload`, `ImageFile`.

**Scene data.** `core/gfx/`: `Light`, `Material`, `Meshlet`, `PrimitiveGen`, `MeshletBuilder`, `ClusterGrid`, `HiZ`, `Portal`, `Probe`, `Decal`. `core/asset/`: `SceneBlob`, `AssimpImporter` (FBX/glTF, meshoptimizer LODs on the job pool). `core/scene/TestScene.hpp`. `core/stream/`: `StreamQueue`, `ResidencyTable`, `StreamRing`. `core/debug/DebugStats.hpp`. `core/text/TextLayout.hpp`. `core/anim/Animation.hpp`. `core/ui/PropertyInspector.hpp`. `core/input/InputQueue.hpp`.

**UI core.** `core/ui/`: `Layout` (`UiBin`), `LayoutBridge` (Yoga), `State`, `Canvas`, `Font`, `PrimitiveBatch`. `Motion.cpp` ticks color transitions and GIF frames. `core/ui/rhi/UiRenderer`. Infrastructure also: `Node`, `Hit`, `Focus`, `Text`.

**Widgets.** `core/ui/widget/`: `Detail` (token and scroll helpers; not a mega-header), `Button`, `Field`, `TextEdit`, `Slider`, `Scroll`, `Virtual`, `VirtualGrid`, `TreeView`, `Splitter`, `Menu`, `Image`, `Breadcrumbs`, `Rubberband`, `Curve`, `Tip`, `List`, `Chrome`, `Docking`, `Panel`. `core/ui/kit/`: `Calendar`, `Color` / `ColorPicker`.

**Tools.** `core/ui/Domain.hpp`. `core/host/Host.hpp`. `core/files/`: `Model`, `Format`, `FileDomain`, `Browser`, `Files`, `Project`. `core/Units.hpp`.

---

## 10. Verification

A code change is done only when every line holds:

1. Dependencies point downward. No `rhi` → window types, no UI core → widgets, no UI → tools, no render pass → `ui/Model.hpp`.
2. No second JSON parser, string helper, input queue, virtualizer, or shader-math copy.
3. `Tick`, `Layout`, `Emit`, `Draw`, `Consume`, and `HitTest` do not allocate.
4. Hot structs are aligned PODs addressed by id. No magic tags, fake fixed arrays, or function-local `static` mutables.
5. UI color comes from `paintToken`. Layer 3 uses the facades in §2.
6. Intermediate image barriers keep `discard = false`. One SPIR-V per pass family. Resize recreates transient targets only.
7. No unguarded POSIX headers, `getenv("HOME")`, or hardcoded asset roots.
8. Existing behavior (menus, rename, rubberband, modifiers, history, docking) is still present.

After any code edit, both targets must compile and the tests must pass:

```bash
cmake --build build-core --target BurnhopeTest BurnhopeEngine -j && ./build-core/BurnhopeTest
```

Zero warnings on the C++26 toolchain in use. Do not dump `git diff` or whole files into the chat; apply the edit directly.
NEVER emit glyphs with the widget box after a failed scroll intersection (causes inspector text over the file pane); ALWAYS skip the run when the clip rect is empty.
NEVER try_get an empty Flecs tag (UiSplitter, UiMenuBar, UiResizable) (returns nullptr and the hit is dropped); ALWAYS entity.has<Tag>().
NEVER parent a property section header into the split row (disclosure sits right of the grip and labels get no width); ALWAYS a full-width header above its rows and one shared label width.
NEVER let a splitter grip consume a press that already hit another focusable control (toolbar buttons stop firing); ALWAYS ignore the grip when the hit is a different focusable node.
NEVER emit UiText from the generic pass on a UiTextInput node (field glyphs draw twice over the caret); ALWAYS let the field decor own that run.
NEVER join the breadcrumb root leaf into the clicked path again (segment clicks open a doubled folder); ALWAYS treat the first segment as the root when root is set.
NEVER scan every node to park an inline editor (the live row is already in the virtual pool); ALWAYS place the field from that slot.
NEVER bind file icons at local photo indices 6 and 7 (those collide with the tail of the eight-slot photo heap); ALWAYS store heap slots 662 and 663 and pass slot - kUiDescPhoto (1 byte index, range 0..7).
NEVER publish a radiance cascade index with vkCmdUpdateBuffer (stalls the queue and is banned in §7); ALWAYS a 16-byte RcPushConstants block, cascade in dword 0.
NEVER keep sparse radiance probes in one HeapBuf::Rc copy across two frames in flight (the hash races and a moving camera fills the cap); ALWAYS two 256-byte-aligned slices, flight in bit 0 of the push, cleared before allocation.
NEVER leave an unsampled Split RC direction at radiance 0 (black cones survive the merge); ALWAYS Beta = 1 and the parent average when the ray count is 0.
NEVER run Split RC atomics in host-visible memory (each add crosses the bus and the frame stalls); ALWAYS a device-local HeapBuf::Rc arena at slot 18, one staging copy of the 256-byte header and positions.
NEVER pick a Split RC ray from the atomic claim order or a per-frame R2 offset (the same pixel changes direction every frame and the GI strobes); ALWAYS R2 of the pixel coordinate times the ray count, stable while the camera is still.
NEVER hash a radiance probe from the low bits of X alone (a wall column shares one chain of 32 and half the cells drop or strobe as the camera turns); ALWAYS mix x, y, z and lod, with c0 cap 32768 and hash 131072.
NEVER start a Split RC ray with a cell-sized bias or leave c0 direction bins empty (the contact gap is skipped and the parent sky fills the shadow); ALWAYS a 1 cm offset from the stored surface, all 32 directions, β = 0 on a hit, and a second bounce from the merged irradiance.
NEVER resolve a packed texture only as `{bhop}/name` (a one-letter prefix misses the content folder and the model shows the wrong picture); ALWAYS the leaf after `X/`, then a depth-4 walk from the working directory and the executable's project that skips cache and build.
NEVER take the first CAS writer as a radiance probe origin (the two flights pick different surfaces and the same cell flashes bright and dark); ALWAYS atomicMin of the pixel index at meta+28, initialized to 0xFFFFFFFF, and rebuild the point from that pixel's depth.
NEVER deposit a back-facing Split RC bin as valid black or a hit as sun-only zero (the cosine mix becomes a flat shadow with no bounce); ALWAYS leave the back bin unsampled, and on a hit write albedo times shadowed sun plus sky, darker when the hit distance is under t0.
NEVER multiply the sky LUT by a sun gradient or add a second sun disk in shade_sky (the disk is already in the LUT and the glow washes out the clouds); ALWAYS write the LUT sample, and composite clouds in debug modes 0 and 4.
NEVER divide a Split RC parent by four empty siblings (one far hit becomes 1/64 by c0 and the bounce is only a shadow); ALWAYS the mean of the children whose valid flag is set.
NEVER add unshadowed sky onto a Split RC hit (sun and sky clamp to the same ceiling and the GI goes flat white); ALWAYS J = albedo times shadowed sun plus the previous bounce with β = 0, and sky only on a miss at the last cascade.
NEVER mark an untraced Split RC bin valid with β = 1 (the parent sky fills every direction the ray never measured and GI is only light); ALWAYS valid = 0 when count = 0, I = J + β·parent only for a measured bin, and sun visibility from the cascade shadow map at the hit.
NEVER shade a Split RC hit from the triangle normal alone (brick normal-map shadows and the sun PBR term are dropped and the bounce is flat); ALWAYS read hdrDirect when the hit matches the screen depth, and compute sun times the shadow map only off screen.
NEVER reject a Split RC screen hit on a 6 cm test or replace hdr in GI debug (a one-texel miss stores the flat normal, lamps are skipped, and the view is only the bounce); ALWAYS a 5×5 view-depth match, a depth march when the BLAS misses, lamps in debug modes 0 and 4, and the cascade added on top of that hdr.
NEVER show Split RC debug as hdrDirect plus bounce (Lit and GI become the same picture and the receiver albedo hides color bleeding); ALWAYS debug mode 4 writes irradiance times white 0.8 with direct sun omitted, while the trace still reads the shaded hdr from before that replace.
NEVER show a property page by the scroll inner (uiShowOnly hides the wrong siblings and Sun stays on the post page); ALWAYS show and hide the scroll view that is the direct child of the inspector.
NEVER emit a wall with vertex normal (0,1,0) (shade replaces the face normal and every wall is lit as a floor); ALWAYS write the face normal on each quad vertex, 12 bytes xyz.
NEVER call uiText on a menu button that already owns a caption child (Yoga throws: a measured node cannot have children); ALWAYS write that caption child, and skip the measure function when the yoga node has children.
NEVER cap a Split RC BLAS at 3000000 triangles (the tail, including the color cubes, is missing and every ray misses into the sky); ALWAYS bake each triangle whose indices sit inside the vertex and index buffers.
NEVER add sky fill or an env reflection into HdrA while world radiance cascades run (every hit bakes blue and GI is a sky wash); ALWAYS direct sun, the cascade shadow, and lamps in that image, and sky only on a miss of the last cascade.
NEVER start a Split RC ray along the shading normal (a normal map aims into the triangle, the ray misses, and the bin fills with sky); ALWAYS 1 cm along the depth normal, 12 bytes xyz.
NEVER write the sky LUT into a Split RC miss (the LUT is tens of units and GI becomes a white field); ALWAYS J = 0 on a miss, and divide a shaded hit by sun intensity so albedo and the shadow stay in 0..1.
NEVER store a Split RC miss as a measured black bin (the empty direction is averaged in and GI is a gray field with black spots); ALWAYS leave that bin unmeasured, and on a hit write albedo times sun visibility, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER read a Split RC hit from a screen pixel or anchor the probe to that pixel (the cube is red only at point-blank and the rest is gray baseColor times the sun); ALWAYS a 48-byte world vertex, UV plus normal, albedo texture and the cascade shadow at the hit, probe rays from the surface stored at meta+32.
NEVER trace a Split RC probe from the empty cell center (the ray starts inside the mesh, every hit is dropped, and GI is black); ALWAYS from that surface, 12 bytes xyz and 12 bytes normal, and keep baseColor when the albedo sample is empty.
NEVER push a Split RC shadow sample 5 cm along the normal (the point sinks under the triangle and the cascade map returns fully shadowed, so GI is black); ALWAYS sample the shadow map at the hit, biased only by the sun texel slope, with the normal facing out of the triangle.
NEVER take Split RC sun visibility from the cascade map on a world hit (a point outside the frustum reads the dark edge and J is stored as zero); ALWAYS a ray toward the sun, origin 2 cm along the outward normal, TMin 5 cm, and scale J by the sun intensity, 4 bytes.
NEVER trace a Split RC ray against the BLAS (the query returns no hit and every probe stays black); ALWAYS one identity TLAS instance, mask 0xFF, its device address at header byte 112, 8 bytes.
NEVER keep a far Split RC hit only on the parent cascade (c0 stays empty and the city is black); ALWAYS write that hit's radiance into the shooting probe's cascade 0, 12 bytes rgb, β = 0.
NEVER choose the Split RC cell from distance to the camera (far surfaces leave the fine grid and only a point-blank hit stays colored); ALWAYS lod 0 and spacing baseSpacing, one world grid.
NEVER allocate a 0.45 m Split RC cell for every pixel of a city view (the hash overflows and black squares flicker); ALWAYS world spacing Δs·2^n at the surface, the same hit radiance in that cell and the next coarser cell, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER pick a Split RC cell from the camera or clamp the ray length to 16 m (the same wall changes brightness as you walk, and the length slider does nothing); ALWAYS floor(world / spacing) with lod 0, and the ray TMax from push baseLength, 4 bytes.
NEVER keep a Split RC hit closer than 5 cm (the ray strikes the surface it started on, Le is 0, and the cell under the camera is a black square); ALWAYS continue that ray, and take the normal from surf1 oriented toward the camera, 12 bytes.
NEVER choose a Split RC origin by the winning screen pixel or flip its normal toward the camera (the grid swims as you move and a grazing view goes black); ALWAYS the surface closest to the world cell center, its surf1 normal, 12 bytes xyz.
NEVER drop a fine Split RC cell to black when the hash is full (0.1 m overflows and the square vanishes as the camera turns); ALWAYS the world cell at 4× spacing, inserted before the fine one, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER deposit a zero Split RC hit as a measured bin (a black square sits between lit cells and its count changes with the camera); ALWAYS leave that bin empty and shade from the next world cell that has light, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER rebuild Split RC from screen pixels every frame (the yellow and blue cubes swap with the camera, uncovered cells go black, and the slice clear stalls the queue); ALWAYS bake each flight once from every triangle into its 256-byte-aligned slice, intervals t0·4^n with t0 in the push, J = albedo·N·L·sunVis in 0..1, shade multiplies by the receiver albedo.
NEVER park a Split RC hit only on a parent cascade or walk 256 cells per triangle axis (the merge drops the bounce so Lit is only albedo, and the atomic walk freezes the machine for a minute); ALWAYS deposit J on cascade 0 of the shooting probe, 12 bytes rgb, and at most 32 steps per axis.
NEVER stride Split RC probes across a triangle or paint the receiver albedo when the lookup misses (trilinear only sees the next cell, so GI is a flat dark color); ALWAYS a probe in every cell while the bbox product is within 16384, J on cascade n for t in (t_{n-1}, t_n] with t_n = 1.6·Δs·4^n and β = 1 on each lower cascade, and I = J + β·(sum of the four children)/4.
NEVER revoxelize a VXGI clipmap whose camera voxel did not change (the volume is rewritten every frame and the light swims); ALWAYS three 128³ tori, two flights, scroll in the 64-byte cascade block, and only the slab that entered.
NEVER scale outdoor sky ambient by the GI gain (GI off and VXGI store radiance 0 in shadow and the albedo vanishes); ALWAYS albedo times sky chroma times sun intensity 0.16, 12 bytes rgb, and leave that term at 0 while radiance cascades run.
NEVER shade a cloud shadow from a 2D hash (the blotch misses the cloud in the sky); ALWAYS the same Worley sample as cloudMarch, six taps along the sun ray through cloudBottom..cloudTop, transmittance in 0.42..1.
NEVER resolve a VXGI atom by the linear voxel id (the scroll torus writes a different texel and the street breaks a few meters from the camera); ALWAYS the scrolled texel, 16 bytes rgba.
NEVER voxelize VXGI from one mip-2 albedo for the whole triangle (the bounce is a flat wash and bricks disappear); ALWAYS a barycentric UV, normal map and ORM per voxel, lod 0 on the 0.125 m cascade, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER show a radiance-cascade pixel without sky chroma (Lit and GI stay gray in shadow); ALWAYS add albedo times sky chroma times sun intensity 0.16 in rc_shade after the probe sum, 12 bytes rgb, and keep that term out of the trace input.
NEVER pow an XeGTAO visibility again in shade (FinalValuePower already shapes the contact and a second pow only darkens); ALWAYS lerp(1, visibility, strength) times material AO, 4 bytes.
NEVER divide the XeGTAO denoise result by 1.5 again or floor it with lerp(0.55, 1) and a 0.35 direct factor (open pixels become 0.67 and every shadow just gets darker); ALWAYS saturate(packed/255) and multiply diffuse and sky ambient by that visibility, 4 bytes.
NEVER destroy FSR targets while the other flight fence is unsignaled (the device is lost and recovery snaps the button back to Native); ALWAYS vkWaitForFences on that flight, 500 ms, then recreate, and log quality plus both extents.
NEVER leave kUiCmdCap at 48 (the file menu plus FSR fills it and Цветокор opens with zero children, height 12); ALWAYS 128 command slots.
NEVER dispatch a scene pass at the swapchain extent while FSR has resized the targets (the render area is larger than the image and the device is lost); ALWAYS scene extent for the pass and gFrame.extent, display size in padExt, 8 bytes.
NEVER add FSR jitter X with the same sign as the Halton sample (m[8] shifts NDC by minus that value, the frame shakes and history misses); ALWAYS NDC x = -2·jx/width and NDC y = +2·jy/height, 8 bytes.
NEVER aim a ReSTIR shadow ray at the attenuation radius (an 8 m disk misses the occluder and the penumbra never forms); ALWAYS a point on the 0.15 m source disk, last 4 bytes of the light, TMax to that point.
NEVER rotate the XeGTAO Hilbert angle with the frame index (denoise above zero swims forever and denoise zero is only a frozen dither); ALWAYS NoiseIndex 0, and denoise 0..3 maps beta 10000, 1.2, 0.55, 0.22, 4 bytes.
NEVER attenuate a point light with saturate(1 - dist/radius)^2 plus a 0.35 m core (the falloff is a blob and the center is a fake hotspot); ALWAYS Filament windowed inverse-square, smoothFactor^2 / max(dist^2, 1e-4), 4 bytes.
NEVER compare a point shadow as one texel (the edge is a hard cut); ALWAYS a 5-tap blocker search and a 3x3 PCF whose radius is sourceRadius * (receiver - blocker) / (blocker * range), clamped to 1..8 texels of the 512 map.
NEVER march fog in 16 steps out to 64 m (the volume is banded and the far air is missing); ALWAYS the Wenzel height integral (atCam - atEnd) / (falloff * view.y) times the ray length, Beer-Lambert, one sun inscatter.
NEVER add the sky LUT or a secondary direct sample into the SHaRC query image (the LUT is tens of units, one lamp sample blacks the pixel, and Lit becomes the GI); ALWAYS one cosine ray and SharcGetCachedRadiance, RELAX before albedo.
NEVER store a SHaRC miss as sky chroma (the hue of the LUT paints every cell red and the object color is gone); ALWAYS add 0 on a miss, 12 bytes rgb, and keep the hit direct in the cell.
NEVER InterlockedAdd SHaRC radiance through uint4.y or uint4.z (the component atomic stays on R and G and B stay 0); ALWAYS a 16-byte voxel, byte offsets 0, 4, 8 and 12.
NEVER sample an sRGB albedo as UNORM or tonemap Rec.709 through the Rec.2020 AgX inset with a saturated sky at 0.16 of the sun (midtones lift, greens go cyan, and the frame burns white); ALWAYS BC*_SRGB on color maps, the Rec.709 inset, noon sun (1, 0.92, 0.76), a pale sky fill at 0.055 of the sun, and one EV before AgX, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER pack a SHaRC voxel as two fp16 pairs or hold the screen history at a fixed 0.92 blend (G and B quantize to 0 and the first red sample stays); ALWAYS a 32-byte record with 12 bytes rgb as float, history weight histLen/(histLen+1), and five a-trous steps 1, 2, 4, 8, 16.
NEVER drop a SHaRC history sample whose chroma differs, or skip an a-trous tap when the center pixel is empty (the first red hit locks and the holes stay black); ALWAYS a variance clamp around the 3x3 mean, and fill an empty center from neighbors by normal and depth, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER march SSR with a fixed step or flip Y, or fill a miss from the world cubemap (thin hits are skipped, the reflection is upside down, and the RT stub is hidden); ALWAYS the FFX hierarchical march on the reverse-Z MAX atlas, roughness above 0.75 stays dark, and a miss writes confidence 0, 16 bytes rgba.
NEVER abort the SSR Hi-Z march when the mip climbs past 5 (a street-length ray dies and metal stays black); ALWAYS clamp at the coarsest atlas mip and keep advancing, and sample VNDF above roughness 0.06, 16 bytes rgba.
NEVER keep the first SSR hit that still lies on the reflecting plane (a close mirror samples itself and stays black, and the same face pops in and out while the camera moves); ALWAYS step past that plane and accept the hit only after the march refines below mip 0, 16 bytes rgba.
NEVER put a mirror at the bounding-sphere center plus its radius, or sample GGX on roughness 0.045 (the cube hangs beside the canopy and a pure metal stays black); ALWAYS the lowest vertices of the tree, 2 m to the side, the cube bottom on the ground, and a perfect reflection at or below 0.06, 12 bytes xyz.
NEVER reject an SSR hit for lying 8 cm off the reflector or replace a bound ORM with a luminance peak (the cube writes black and imported roughness stays a flat 0.22 while metal stays 1); ALWAYS the FFX 2 px self test, roughness from ORM green and metal from ORM blue, and on a miss one opaque TLAS ray shaded from that pixel's HDR or from SHaRC plus the sky, 16 bytes rgba.
NEVER feed perceptual roughness into the SSR GGX lobe or replace a metal pixel with a missed sample (the mirror stays empty and a roughness of 0.74 is killed by a second gloss); ALWAYS alpha = roughness squared from surf, and add Fresnel on the shaded color, 16 bytes rgba.
NEVER multiply a SHaRC cache hit by the receiver albedo again or accept it inside the voxel (G and B collapse and the bounce is red noise); ALWAYS distance above voxelSize * sqrt(3), footprint above the voxel, and one BRDF throughput times SharcGetCachedRadiance, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER store a SHaRC miss or a shadowed hit as 0 or as the sky LUT, and never multiply that sample by the sun hue (the voxel averages toward black and the bounce goes red); ALWAYS the pale sky (0.78, 0.82, 0.88) times sun intensity 0.055, sun luminance on white, and skip a sample whose luma is 0, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER take SHaRC sun visibility from the ReSTIR screen sample (the raw GI goes black and the denoiser locks a red field); ALWAYS the opaque sun ray and sharcSunEnergy, and that same query color into HdrA when the denoiser is off, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER drop a SHaRC denoise tap by luma or divide the sample by albedo without multiplying that same floor back (green dies and the frame stays red, and the history resets); ALWAYS filter irradiance divided by max(albedo, 0.05), clamp history to the 3x3 min and max, normal power 128, and multiply that floor back into HdrA, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER keep the SHaRC denoise images as untyped RGBA32 storage (the write keeps only R, history alpha stays 0, the frame is red and the speckle never settles); ALWAYS R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT with rgba16f on the image, and composite the same per-channel add the query writes when the denoiser is off, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER clamp SHaRC history to the 3x3 min and max (the brightest red firefly becomes the ceiling and the blur paints the frame red); ALWAYS the same-surface 3x3 mean plus or minus one standard deviation per channel, normal power 128, 12 bytes rgb.
NEVER hand the SHaRC denoise a storage image of the add (G and B come back 0 and the frame is red); ALWAYS the same add.r add.g add.b the query stores into HdrA, 16-byte record, byte offsets 0, 4 and 8, written back per channel, 12 bytes rgb.
